module gunbc.guarantee_stall.text_carrier_render_not_keyed_on_identity_stall

import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, AwaitsOneGrounding, BoundedPopulation, climbs_when }

data text_carrier_render_not_keyed_on_identity_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "Two authorities answer whether a type is host text. The checker decides it by DECLARATION IDENTITY (v1.compiler.infer_env text_representation_by_identity, gunbc.rung_drop text_boundary_identity_wall); the Rust renderer decides which carrier to emit by the authored spelling plus kernel provenance (v1.compiler.emit_rust is_host_text_carrier_type). Nothing forces the two answers to agree: on the self-host path a disagreement surfaces only as a rustc type mismatch in the emitted-crate build, and on any other emission nothing observes it. Nothing fell -- the renderer was provenance-keyed before the checker climbed -- so this is a stall below its ceiling, not a drop (review 72772).",
  current: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: StructurallyImpossible,
  blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding { grounding: "the Rust render paths carry the TypeEnv the checker judged with; four of the deciding paths (v1.compiler.emit_rust render_rust_type, render_rust_type_without_applied_binding, rust_operand_realization_of_type, data_def_annotation_is_named_refinement) take no env, so they cannot ask the identity classifier. THAT ENV IS NOT ENOUGH, MEASURED 2026-10-03 (neat-raven-383, test.claim.bare_imported_text_reading_witness_test): the CHECKER itself reads a bare-imported v2.std.text String as host text -- `import v2.std.text { String }` then `string_length(s: t)` and `concat(t, t)` are ADMITTED, while the qualified `t: v2.std.text.String` into the same primitive REFUSES. So the fork is not renderer-versus-checker: the bare imported spelling reads as host in BOTH authorities, and handing the renderer the checker's answer would hand it the same wrong answer. The climb is four programs, in this order, each with its own trigger: (1) RESOLVER IDENTITY -- a bare imported type reference carries its declaration identity, so text_representation_by_identity reads a bare imported v2 String as CodePointSequence; trigger: the bare-import fixture above refuses while the kernel-String control stays admitted; this is gunbc.rung_drop text_boundary_identity_wall's unidentified-population trigger. (2) DISPOSITION OF THE SURFACED CROSSINGS -- once (1) lands, every src/v2 module that imports v2.std.text String and applies a host-text builtin to it becomes a refused crossing (the population is whatever the checker refuses with (1) in place, not a figure recorded here), dispositioned by a std.coercion conversion-plan route call (unicode_scalar_unfold / unicode_scalar_fold), a structural op in v2.std.text, or a retype to kernel String; trigger: the self-host and dag closures accept with (1) in place. (3) RENDER ENV THREADING -- the four env-less render paths take the TypeEnv and is_host_text_carrier_type is deleted with no fallback arm; trigger: this row's next_rung_trigger below. (4) INTERPRETER REPRESENTATION -- the seed interpreter carries structural text as Str, a Cons/Empty free monoid or a Value::List by PRODUCER, not by declaration, and accepts Value::List nowhere a host string is read; it is keyed on declaration only by evaluating the typed conversion (the route functions) rather than accommodating representations; trigger: no expect_str_free_monoid-style accommodation remains on a text path." },
  population: BoundedPopulation { members: [
    "v1.compiler.infer_env.text_representation_by_identity",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.is_host_text_carrier_type",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.render_rust_type",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.render_rust_applied_type",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.render_rust_decl_type",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.render_rust_fn_sig_type",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.render_rust_type_with_applied_binding_in_scope",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.render_rust_type_without_applied_binding",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.rust_operand_realization_of_type",
    "v1.compiler.emit_rust.data_def_annotation_is_named_refinement"
  ] },
  next_rung_trigger: climbs_when(capability: "every Rust render path that chooses a text carrier reads v1.compiler.infer_env text_representation_by_identity through the TypeEnv it was checked in, SUFFICIENT FOR is_host_text_carrier_type to be deleted with no fallback arm: an unidentified type refuses at render rather than defaulting to a carrier, which in turn needs gunbc.rung_drop text_boundary_identity_wall's resolver trigger (declaration identity on every type reference). Routing only the renderers that already hold an env does not retire this row.")
}
